  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hospital Bond Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The transaction involves a debt investment in 5-year local currency bonds of up to GEL20,000,000 (or its equivalent in US dollars) from the ordinary capital resources of the Asian Development Bank to be issued by JSC Evex Hospitals (Evex Hospitals) for the Hospital Bond Project in Georgia. The project supports Georgia&apos;s capital market development, particularly the deepening of its corporate debt securities market and overall local currency bond market. This transaction also supports Georgia&apos;s universal health care (UHC) program to ensure Georgians can afford access to better health care. This project supports sustaining the supply of quality hospital services, provided by quality health care providers such as Evex Hospitals, to meet growing patient demand for high quality health care services.</narrative>
  </description>
